### mara-api examples
### Runnable with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ's HTTP
### Client. Assumes a `mara-api` process is running against a `mara.toml`
### with `[http] listen = "127.0.0.1:7701"` (see the README's *HTTP API*
### section). If `[auth] enabled = true`, uncomment the Authorization
### header on every request and set @token to a real bearer token minted
### against the daemon's token store.
###
### Two collections, kept deliberately separate: `vecs` (dim 3) for the
### raw-vector examples, runnable with no embedding model configured at
### all; `docs` (dim 384, matching `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`
### — see the README) for the text/chunk-and-insert examples, which need
### `[embedding] model` set in the daemon's own config.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:7701
@token = mara_pat_replace_me

### Health check — no auth required, always answers.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/health

### The full OpenAPI 3.1 spec for this running instance.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/openapi.json

### --- raw-vector examples (`vecs`, dim 3, no embedding model needed) ---

### Create a collection. `metric` defaults to "cosine" if omitted;
### `schema` declares typed payload fields for filtering (omit entirely
### for an unfiltered/untyped collection).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "vecs",
  "dim": 3,
  "metric": "cosine",
  "schema": [
    { "name": "source", "field_type": "keyword" }
  ]
}

### Insert or update one row by key — PUT, since this is an idempotent
### upsert. Either `vector` or `text` is required; `text` with no
### `vector` embeds locally on the daemon side (needs a configured model
### whose output dimension matches the collection's).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/vecs/rows/row-1
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "vector": [0.1, 0.2, 0.3],
  "fields": {
    "source": { "keyword": "manual-insert" }
  }
}

### Fetch one row by key.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/vecs/rows/row-1
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Insert several rows in one request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/vecs/rows/batch
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "items": [
    { "key": "row-2", "vector": [0.4, 0.5, 0.6], "fields": {}, "extra": null },
    { "key": "row-3", "vector": [0.7, 0.8, 0.9], "fields": {}, "extra": null }
  ]
}

### Delete a row by key — 204 No Content on success.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/vecs/rows/row-3
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Vector-only search with an explicit query vector and a filter — no
### local embedding needed since `query_vector` is given directly.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/vecs/search
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "query_vector": [0.1, 0.2, 0.3],
  "mode": "vector_only",
  "k": 5,
  "filter": {
    "eq": { "field": "source", "value": { "str": "manual-insert" } }
  }
}

### Build or rebuild a vector/BM25 index for the collection from current
### storage state. `index_kind`: "flat" | "ivf_pq" | "lsh" | "bm25".
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/vecs/reindex
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "index_kind": "ivf_pq"
}

### --- text/embedding examples (`docs`, dim 384, needs [embedding] model) ---

### A collection sized for `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`'s
### 384-dimensional output — see the README's *Embedding model* section
### for the daemon-side config this requires.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "docs",
  "dim": 384
}

### Chunk-and-insert: splits `text` per `chunk_spec` (server-side
### markdown/sentence/token/character chunking), embeds every chunk with
### the daemon's configured local model, and commits the whole document
### as one transaction. Omit `chunk_spec` for the default (markdown-
### aware, 512 tokens, 64 overlap).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/docs/documents
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "doc_key": "readme",
  "text": "# mara\n\nA ground-up Rust vector database.\n\n## Replication\n\nLeader-follower, async.",
  "source": "README.md"
}

### Hybrid search (BM25 + vector, fused via reciprocal rank fusion) — the
### default `mode`, so it can be omitted entirely. `query_text` with no
### `query_vector` embeds locally for the vector arm.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/docs/search
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "query_text": "how does replication work",
  "k": 5
}

### BM25-only search — `query_text` is required, `query_vector` is
### ignored, and no embedding model is needed for this arm alone.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/collections/docs/search
Content-Type: application/json
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "query_text": "replication",
  "mode": "bm25_only",
  "k": 5
}

### --- admin ---

### Recent audit log entries, newest first — Admin-only regardless of
### `[auth] enabled`.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit?limit=20
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
